<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 15 November, from 655 to 1920.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">655 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,371 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Oswiu of Northumbria defeats and kills Penda of Mercia at the Winwaed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Winwaed, probably near Leeds, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu of Northumbria</a> defeated and killed the pagan King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>, and many of Penda's allied kings also died. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a>, the battle marked the effective end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> paganism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-winwaed">Battle of the Winwaed</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1315">1315 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">711 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swiss confederates ambush the Habsburgs at Morgarten</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Men of Schwyz, Uri and Unterwalden ambushed Duke Leopold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>'s army on a narrow path by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ageri">Lake Ägeri</a>. The victory strengthened the young Swiss Confederation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1533">1533 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">493 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francisco Pizarro's Spaniards enter Cusco, the Inca capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Spanish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, sealing their conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. The Spaniards later rebuilt its palaces and temples, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coricancha">Coricancha</a>, on Inca foundations.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1705">1705 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">321 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Habsburg and Danish forces defeat the Kuruc army at Zsibó</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces of the Habsburg Empire, Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and Vojvodian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi">Francis II Rákóczi</a> at Zsibó in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>. Flanked by the Austrian cavalry, the Hungarians were forced to retreat.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rakoczis-war-of-independence">Rákóczi's War of Independence</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress adopts the Articles of Confederation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> approved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/articles-of-confederation">Articles of Confederation</a>, the first constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Ratified in 1781, they gave the central government too little power and were replaced in 1789.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sherman leaves Atlanta on his March to the Sea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After burning much of Atlanta, William T. Sherman's army set off for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a>. Its destruction of railways, crops and property across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> aimed to break the Confederacy's capacity and will to fight.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1889">1889 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A military coup makes Brazil a republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca">Deodoro da Fonseca</a> led a coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> that deposed Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a> and proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. The 64-year-old emperor went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca">Deodoro da Fonseca</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The League of Nations holds its first Assembly</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 41 nations met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> for the first Assembly of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a>. Weakened by the absence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the League failed to prevent the aggression of the 1930s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 15 November <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-pitt-the-elder"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-pitt-the-elder.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Pitt the Elder</span><span class="tp">1708–1778</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-caspar-lavater"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-caspar-lavater.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johann Caspar Lavater</span><span class="tp">1741–1801</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jerome-bonaparte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jerome-bonaparte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jérôme Bonaparte</span><span class="tp">1784–1860</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/claus-von-stauffenberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Claus von Stauffenberg</span><span class="tp">1907–1944</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mwai-kibaki"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Mwai Kibaki</span><span class="tp">1931–2022</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 15 November <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/penda-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Penda of Mercia</span><span class="tp">d. 655</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/odo-ii-of-blois"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Odo II of Blois</span><span class="tp">985–1037</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-iii-margrave-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-iii-margrave-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leopold III, Margrave of Austria</span><span class="tp">1073–1136</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albertus-magnus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albertus-magnus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albertus Magnus</span><span class="tp">c. 1200–1280</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-antonio-orsini-del-balzo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giovanni-antonio-orsini-del-balzo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giovanni Antonio Orsini del Balzo</span><span class="tp">d. 1463</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johannes-kepler.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johannes Kepler</span><span class="tp">1571–1630</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-amos-comenius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-amos-comenius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Amos Comenius</span><span class="tp">1592–1670</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christoph-willibald-gluck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christoph-willibald-gluck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christoph Willibald Gluck</span><span class="tp">1714–1787</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maria-ii-of-portugal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maria-ii-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maria II of Portugal</span><span class="tp">1819–1853</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henryk-sienkiewicz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henryk-sienkiewicz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henryk Sienkiewicz</span><span class="tp">1846–1916</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
